# Section C, candidate M. Independent reading before the stored fields.
FG-M-02b53098f0 || cls=MX mod=MUST dom=MX rel=PE pol=GOV-017~ conf=M || actor=agent; act=treat product inputs as inputs, not instruction layers; route a product request for an engineering decision through Decision Control; trig=product input asks for engineering decision; scope=root CLAUDE.md; maintenance protocol for instruction layer part; exc=none; time=at decision; enf=text || test=Two claims. Layer status is instruction topology. Decision routing affects work: a spec that asks for Redis cannot override a rule silently. GOV-001 makes the spec authoritative for product behavior only, so routing it is near GOV-017, not a full match.
FG-M-35f716b5eb || cls=UN mod=UNCERTAIN dom=UN rel=UN pol=- conf=L || actor=agent in headless run; act=may an explicit approval in the original request permit a Reserved change; trig=headless run with explicit prompt approval; scope=root CLAUDE.md; exc=none; time=at decision; enf=text || test=Lean: never make a Reserved decision concerns the agent deciding, and an explicit instruction counts as approval, so a prompt approval is not the agent deciding. But proceed only on a non-Reserved path is absolute. GOV-017's silently fits the lean. Text does not settle it.
FG-M-58264ccd7d || cls=UN mod=UNCERTAIN dom=UN rel=UN pol=- conf=L || actor=agent; act=destructive Git allowed when explicitly requested or clearly required by an approved workflow; trig=destructive Git operation; scope=git-workflow skill; exc=approved workflow; time=before operation; enf=text || test=GOV-015 says unless explicitly requested. The approved-workflow branch is not in the oracle. Whether an approved workflow is itself an explicit request cannot be read from either text. Inspection duty is separate.
FG-M-8494a3058e || cls=CD mod=MUST_NOT dom=WF rel=PE pol=DEP-003~ conf=M || actor=checker; act=flag floating or range versions as violations with no explicit-request exception; prerelease only as a note; trig=checker runs; scope=check-manifests script; exc=none for floating; time=when invoked; enf=script finding, execution not verified || test=DEP-003 allows floating when explicitly requested. Checker flags it regardless. Stronger than the policy. Whether a checker should honor it is a design choice for a human.
FG-M-8decaaa9d7 || cls=CD mod=MUST_NOT dom=WF rel=PE pol=GOV-015~ conf=M || actor=agent; act=treat main, master, protected or shared branches as non-rewritable; trig=history rewrite on those branches; scope=git-workflow skill; exc=preceding sentence allows force-push of a shared branch on explicit request; time=before push; enf=text || test=GOV-015 permits force-push on request. Standing alone the second sentence has no exception, so it is stronger. Read with the first sentence, shared branches are in both, so an unconditional reading would empty the first sentence's exception. Exception reach not fully stated.
FG-M-f268d4b313 || cls=XW mod=MUST dom=WF rel=NE pol=- conf=L || actor=harness; act=block Bash and PowerShell if guard cannot run; trig=guard failure; scope=settings.json; exc=none; time=PreToolUse; enf=declared onFailure field, host support not verified || test=Nothing in the oracle requires failing closed. Static reading only: the field is declared, its host effect is not established here. Cannot be resolved without executing.
FG-M-fb96c148bf || cls=MX mod=MUST dom=MX rel=NE pol=- conf=M || actor=scanner; act=findings include severity, location, title, evidence, risk, impact, remediation, OWASP when applicable; report in the prescribed shape; do not duplicate other skills' guidance in the scan; trig=security scan; scope=security-scan skill; exc=OWASP when applicable; time=report; enf=text || test=Report fields and shape are procedure beyond WF-020. The do-not-duplicate sentence is a different action: it could concern the scan output or the instruction system. Different outcomes; compound.
FG-M-fd01a5254d || cls=UN mod=UNCERTAIN dom=UN rel=UN pol=- conf=L || actor=implementer; act=pre-success invalidation acceptable only when workflow deliberately accepts; trig=invalidation before mutation success; scope=caching skill; exc=the deliberate acceptance; time=design; enf=text || test=RUN-021 says consistent with successful mutations. If mutation fails after invalidation the cache just misses, so the cache is not wrong, and RUN-021 might not forbid it. Or the phrase means only after success, making this an exception to it. The oracle phrase does not settle which.
FG-M-fd891d29da || cls=MX mod=MUST_NOT dom=WF rel=PE pol=GOV-015~,GOV-019~,GOV-020~ conf=M || actor=agent; act=listed Git operations only when requested or required by approved workflow, after inspecting what will be lost; trig=high-risk Git; scope=git-workflow skill; exc=explicit request or approved workflow; time=before operation; enf=text || test=Explicit-request branch matches GOV-015. Inspection matches GOV-020. Approved-workflow branch stays open, as for FG-M-58264ccd7d.
